-- title:
--   Lattices of pluricanonical symbols are compatible with formally étale extensions
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $A$, $B$, $K$ be commutative $R$-algebras together with ring homomorphisms $A\to B$, $A\to K$ and $B\to K$ such that all resulting triangles commute (the towers $R\to A\to B$, $A\to B\to K$, $R\to A\to K$ and $R\to B\to K$). Fix $n,m\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $P:=\big(\textstyle\bigwedge^{n}_{K}\Omega_{K/R}\big)^{\otimes_K m}$, with $d\colon K\to\Omega_{K/R}$ the universal derivation. For $C\in\{A,B\}$ let $\Lambda_C\subseteq P$ be the $C$-submodule spanned by all elements
--   $\bigotimes_{j=1}^{m}\big(d\bar c_{j,1}\wedge\cdots\wedge d\bar c_{j,n}\big)$ with $c_{j,i}\in C$, where $\bar c$ denotes the image of $c$ in $K$.
--
--   If $A\to B$ is formally étale, then
--   $$
--   \Lambda_B\;=\;B\cdot\Lambda_A ,
--   $$
--   i.e. the lattice generated by $B$ equals the $B$-submodule of $P$ spanned by the lattice generated by $A$.
--
--   The main application is to a localization $A\to B=A_t$, which is formally étale. When $K$ is the function field of a smooth variety and $A$ is the coordinate ring of an affine open, the statement says that the lattice of regular pluricanonical forms on a basic open set $D(t)$ is the localization of the lattice on the ambient affine open. This is the algebraic input for the locality of regularity of pluricanonical forms.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The lattice $\Lambda_C$ is `rationalLattice R C K n m`; $K$ is only assumed to be a commutative ring. Formal étaleness is `Algebra.FormallyEtale A B`, and the right-hand side is `Submodule.span B` of the underlying set of $\Lambda_A$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/AlgebraicGeometry/LogKodaira/LatticeBaseChange.lean#L197-L216

